  "correction_rules": [
    "Adjust forecasts downward when sentiment is low (≤0.33) and recent prices show mean reversion or downward momentum.",
    "Increase forecast sensitivity to recent spikes (≥70.0) — avoid undershooting after sharp rallies.",
    "Apply lag correction: if true outcome exceeds forecast by >5% over 3 consecutive days, reduce next-day forecast by 1–2%.",
    "When sentiment is high (≥0.50), allow slightly higher forecast bias upward, but cap at +3% above recent 7-day average to prevent overshoot.",
    "If forecast consistently underestimates true outcome in early days of 30d window, shift baseline upward by 0.5–1.5% to account for lagged momentum.",
    "For sentiment = 0.00, assume neutral drift — use 30d moving average as anchor, avoid overreacting to short-term noise."
  ]
}
